From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: athexweb3 <athexweb3@nirapod.org>
Date: Sun, 18 Oct 2026 21:00:53 +0600
Subject: [PATCH] armv8a: changelog entries for the vector registers and the
 SHA instructions

Co-authored-by: orvenweb3 <orvenweb3@gmail.com>
---
 changes/01-feature/1643-armv8a-simd-crypto.md     | 15 +++++++++++++++
 .../02-bugfix/1643-syscall-vector-registers.md    |  9 +++++++++
 2 files changed, 24 insertions(+)
 create mode 100644 changes/01-feature/1643-armv8a-simd-crypto.md
 create mode 100644 changes/02-bugfix/1643-syscall-vector-registers.md

diff --git a/changes/01-feature/1643-armv8a-simd-crypto.md b/changes/01-feature/1643-armv8a-simd-crypto.md
new file mode 100644
index 00000000..b7dc36af
--- /dev/null
+++ b/changes/01-feature/1643-armv8a-simd-crypto.md
@@ -0,0 +1,15 @@
+- armv8a: `u128` values now live in the SIMD&FP registers `v0` to `v31`,
+  passed in `v0` to `v7` and returned in `v0` to `v3` as in AAPCS64, with
+  `v8` to `v15` callee-saved; the bitwise operators, element-wise addition
+  and subtraction, shifts by a constant and the constant zero on `u128`
+  are lowered to Advanced SIMD instructions, and the permutations and
+  element moves (EXT, REV32, REV64, TRN1, TRN2, ZIP1, ZIP2, UZP1, UZP2,
+  DUP, INS, UMOV) are provided as intrinsics. An export function that
+  issues a system call now saves and restores `q8` to `q15`
+  ([PR #1643](https://github.com/jasmin-lang/jasmin/pull/1643)).
+- armv8a: add the SHA-256, SHA-512 and SHA-3 instructions (SHA256H,
+  SHA256H2, SHA256SU0, SHA256SU1, SHA512H, SHA512H2, SHA512SU0, SHA512SU1,
+  EOR3, BCAX, RAX1, XAR) as intrinsics; the compiler does not check that
+  the target implements these optional features, and the assembler has
+  to enable them (for llvm-mc, `-mattr=+sha2,+sha3`)
+  ([PR #1643](https://github.com/jasmin-lang/jasmin/pull/1643)).
diff --git a/changes/02-bugfix/1643-syscall-vector-registers.md b/changes/02-bugfix/1643-syscall-vector-registers.md
new file mode 100644
index 00000000..fe6d649a
--- /dev/null
+++ b/changes/02-bugfix/1643-syscall-vector-registers.md
@@ -0,0 +1,9 @@
+- System calls (e.g., `#randombytes`) are no longer assumed to preserve the
+  vector registers, as the ABIs preserve them only in part. This only changes
+  `-call-conv windows`: an export function that issues a
+  system call, directly or through a local function, now saves and restores
+  `ymm6` to `ymm15` (with AVX instructions, in a 32-byte aligned frame), so it
+  may need a larger `#[callee_saved]` and can no longer use
+  `#[stackalign=u128]`; and a vector value can no longer stay in a register
+  across a system call (spill it explicitly)
+  ([PR #1643](https://github.com/jasmin-lang/jasmin/pull/1643)).
